From 0cc329db1c84918a7fb083146e15c9fc8ff74347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:53:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Trip builder: phone fixes, a quiz that tells the truth,
 and the pay-your-way screens

Synced from the trip builder source (scripts/sync-allin.mjs), so this copy and the source can't drift apart.

Fixes
- "Start from a classic", "Surprise me", "Swap in ALL IN" and similar buttons did nothing when pressed
  from the builder (the address didn't change, so nothing redrew). They work now.
- Phone: stop cards had the hostel name squeezed to one word per line with the nights / move / remove
  controls on top of it. The controls now sit on their own row.
- Phone: the home page scrolled sideways, the "ALL IN" nav button wrapped onto two lines, and the map
  pushed the headline and buttons below the fold. Headline and buttons now lead, map underneath.
- Map: pins sat under the region chips and the zoom buttons. The map now fits into the part you can see.
- The builder panel is much shorter on a phone: festivals and "know before you go" start folded, and the
  Trip Doctor and Don't miss show one item until you ask for more.
- Quiz: a must-do (e.g. the Ha Giang Loop) was silently dropped when the budget was "cheap", and the result
  still said "Best fit". Must-dos now win over the activity price cap; if the budget crowds them out every
  route, the quiz leads with one that has them and says it's a bit over budget; each result says what it
  leaves out. Routes can no longer claim to be inside a budget they're above, and routes linked by land
  or boat beat routes that hop by plane on short trips.
- Copy: one set of words for the deposit ($50 on trips you build vs $99 on ALL IN), driven by config.
- Logos are 60 KB lighter on every first load.

New
- The status page lets the guest choose how to pay the rest once the crew approves (see the payments commit).
- Config: DEPOSIT_PER_PERSON, PAY_ENDPOINT, ALLIN_BASE (the ALL IN prices and links match this site).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
